WEBVTT

00:08.174 --> 00:09.634
Mikey!

00:11.928 --> 00:14.597
At last, it's over.

00:15.724 --> 00:19.728
My life was nothing but suffering.

00:22.480 --> 00:23.565
Takemitchy.

00:25.066 --> 00:26.109
Your hand...

00:28.570 --> 00:29.571
It's so warm.

00:36.661 --> 00:37.579
Takemichi.

00:49.883 --> 00:52.218
TOKYO REVENGERS

02:20.974 --> 02:24.018
This rain sucks. Jeez, it's cold.

02:27.814 --> 02:28.648
Huh?

02:30.191 --> 02:31.609
You bastard!

02:32.402 --> 02:34.445
You won't get the best of me!

02:36.156 --> 02:37.699
What the heck are you doing?

02:38.324 --> 02:41.452
Wh... What're you doing here?

02:41.452 --> 02:43.037
That's a dumb question.

02:43.621 --> 02:45.456
I was on my way to your place

02:45.456 --> 02:48.877
when I saw some moron
getting in a fight with a tire.

02:50.253 --> 02:54.424
Talking to a tire in the rain
is pretty damn creepy, dude.

02:54.424 --> 02:55.675
Screw you!

02:55.675 --> 02:58.511
I'm busy! I don't have time for your crap!

02:58.511 --> 03:01.472
Hey. Is that any way to talk to me?

03:01.472 --> 03:03.641
I'm training right now.

03:04.350 --> 03:06.477
I'm going to be tougher
than anyone around.

03:11.191 --> 03:14.777
Unless I get stronger,
I can't change the future.

03:17.030 --> 03:17.864
Wait.

03:18.489 --> 03:21.492
Are you Takemitchy from the future?

03:26.539 --> 03:28.708
No way!

03:30.460 --> 03:32.587
Everyone's dead?

03:33.421 --> 03:35.882
And it was Mikey who killed them?

03:43.765 --> 03:44.682
You can't be serious.

03:46.226 --> 03:49.395
That's why I've gotta get stronger.

03:50.355 --> 03:52.857
And that's why you're fighting a tire?

03:52.857 --> 03:54.525
What are you? A child?

03:54.525 --> 03:55.526
Screw you!

03:56.152 --> 04:00.615
In the future, I quit Toman,
but everyone stood up for me.

04:00.615 --> 04:03.451
I'm so damn pathetic.

04:07.580 --> 04:09.916
So, if I want to stay in Toman,

04:09.916 --> 04:13.169
I've gotta be tough enough
for everyone to respect me.

04:16.256 --> 04:18.383
Stop! Show me your hands.

04:20.802 --> 04:22.345
They're covered in blood.

04:27.684 --> 04:28.559
No way.

04:29.269 --> 04:32.480
Don't tell me you've been
punching that all day long.

04:35.650 --> 04:37.443
Cut it out, Takemitchy!

04:37.443 --> 04:39.821
If you bust your knuckles doing that,

04:39.821 --> 04:41.489
you won't ever get any stronger.

04:42.407 --> 04:46.327
I thought it over a lot with Naoto.

04:49.455 --> 04:53.001
What can I do in the past
to make the future better

04:54.085 --> 04:56.004
and save everyone?

04:56.879 --> 05:00.300
We ran in circles
trying to find some clue.

05:00.967 --> 05:02.760
Who killed Hina?

05:03.428 --> 05:06.764
Was it really Mikey who killed everyone?

05:10.226 --> 05:12.520
That's enough, Takemitchy.

05:16.566 --> 05:18.484
Cool it, okay?

05:20.486 --> 05:23.114
I couldn't think of anything.

05:24.532 --> 05:27.535
I had no idea how to save everyone.

05:29.078 --> 05:31.080
I didn't know how to help them.

05:32.999 --> 05:37.337
I didn't have... a single freaking clue.

05:39.505 --> 05:40.965
Chifuyu!

05:42.050 --> 05:43.593
This sucks!

05:44.510 --> 05:46.387
It's so disheartening!

05:47.805 --> 05:52.226
Mikey died right in my own hands.

05:53.019 --> 05:56.898
I can still feel him in my hands.

05:58.691 --> 06:00.401
This totally blows!

06:16.250 --> 06:18.544
That's a pretty shitty future.

06:20.171 --> 06:21.005
But you know,

06:21.881 --> 06:23.549
I'm honestly pretty happy.

06:24.092 --> 06:24.967
Huh?

06:25.551 --> 06:28.137
I mean, we're able to meet again.

06:31.015 --> 06:34.310
I totally thought
we'd never see each other again.

06:42.693 --> 06:45.988
I have a feeling I know what I gotta do.

06:45.988 --> 06:46.906
Really?

06:50.034 --> 06:52.453
I'll beat the crap out of Mikey.

06:53.538 --> 06:54.414
Huh?

06:55.289 --> 06:57.083
Are you insane?

06:57.083 --> 06:58.209
He'll kill you.

06:58.209 --> 07:00.920
Yeah. He's going to kill me anyway.

07:00.920 --> 07:03.673
That's not what I mean.

07:03.673 --> 07:04.799
I mean, don't be stupid.

07:05.758 --> 07:09.971
It really ticks me off to think
that I'll just let him kill me.

07:11.764 --> 07:13.683
Mikey's just so tough,

07:13.683 --> 07:16.561
nobody's ever seriously taken him on.

07:18.438 --> 07:24.193
The only people who are willing to really
take on the invincible Mikey head-on...

07:25.236 --> 07:26.737
are probably just you and me.

07:35.913 --> 07:36.747
Oh.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.376
The rain's stopped.

07:42.628 --> 07:44.005
Thanks, Chifuyu.

07:44.672 --> 07:45.923
I feel better now.

07:47.300 --> 07:52.221
"Mikey's just so tough,
nobody's ever seriously taken him on."

07:53.723 --> 07:57.310
I had convinced myself
that there was nothing I could do.

07:57.810 --> 08:02.148
I believed Mikey was on a different level
and I wasn't like him.

08:03.357 --> 08:04.192
I know how you feel.

08:05.193 --> 08:07.236
But that's not true.

08:08.321 --> 08:09.864
He's a friend.

08:10.656 --> 08:13.159
When Baji left Toman,

08:13.159 --> 08:17.038
he didn't say he would destroy Valhalla,
but that he was bringing Baji back.

08:17.747 --> 08:18.581
Yeah.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.709
Mikey's always put his friends first.

08:22.210 --> 08:23.044
Yeah.

08:23.544 --> 08:25.254
Mikey told me,

08:26.422 --> 08:29.592
"My life was nothing but suffering."

08:31.719 --> 08:34.138
If he's suffering,
I'll do everything I can to support him.

08:34.722 --> 08:36.641
If he's in the wrong,
I'll take him on seriously.

08:37.141 --> 08:40.770
That's the kind of friend
I want to be for Mikey.

08:41.771 --> 08:42.605
Right.

08:43.523 --> 08:45.024
I've made up my mind, Chifuyu.

08:47.026 --> 08:50.988
I'm never going back to the future
until I'm the leader of Toman.

08:54.408 --> 08:57.161
<i>Mikey... and all you guys...</i>

08:58.538 --> 09:01.582
This will be my final revenge.

09:03.167 --> 09:05.336
All right. Let's do this!

09:09.549 --> 09:12.009
I'll be right there with you, partner.

09:20.434 --> 09:22.186
This really warms me up.

09:22.186 --> 09:23.938
- Ow!
- Huh?

09:24.605 --> 09:25.898
My hands sting.

09:26.440 --> 09:29.652
Of course they'd hurt. Idiot.

09:30.444 --> 09:32.780
So, what're we going to do?

09:33.322 --> 09:36.367
Just taking on Mikey
won't change anything.

09:36.367 --> 09:37.910
Can't argue with that.

09:38.619 --> 09:41.247
If only there was a war.

09:41.247 --> 09:42.164
What?

09:42.164 --> 09:43.666
Don't you get it?

09:43.666 --> 09:45.960
I could do something cool,
gain everyone's respect,

09:45.960 --> 09:48.004
and become Toman's leader.

09:50.715 --> 09:51.674
Show some modesty.

09:52.883 --> 09:55.094
I was just being hypothetical.

09:58.055 --> 10:02.018
I really wonder
why Mikey turned out like that.

10:02.018 --> 10:02.977
Huh?

10:02.977 --> 10:05.605
I mean, it makes no sense.

10:05.605 --> 10:08.232
Can a guy change that much
in just 12 years?

10:10.276 --> 10:13.946
It goes to show just how deep
the darkness in his heart was.

10:15.197 --> 10:16.032
Darkness?

10:16.532 --> 10:17.992
I'm not sure,

10:17.992 --> 10:21.078
but something must have
triggered the change in him.

10:22.747 --> 10:23.831
A trigger...

10:25.791 --> 10:26.667
What about Kisaki?

10:26.667 --> 10:27.752
Huh?

10:27.752 --> 10:33.549
The biggest change this last time was that
Kisaki got kicked out of Toman, right?

10:34.967 --> 10:39.639
Are you saying that Mikey needs Kisaki?

10:39.639 --> 10:41.265
Well, yeah.

10:41.265 --> 10:44.268
The hell he does. That guy's a douchebag.

10:44.268 --> 10:49.398
But in the previous timeline,
Kisaki represented the darkness in Toman.

10:49.398 --> 10:54.654
Kisaki's departure from Toman could be
one of the triggers that changes Mikey.

10:55.237 --> 10:56.405
Good point.

10:57.657 --> 11:00.576
Kisaki might even know something.

11:01.160 --> 11:01.994
Yeah.

11:02.870 --> 11:07.458
YOKOHAMA

11:12.880 --> 11:14.340
I feel heaviness in the air.

11:16.550 --> 11:19.345
Something always happens
on days like today.

11:21.222 --> 11:23.182
And then you showed up.

11:24.725 --> 11:25.726
Kisaki.

11:33.484 --> 11:34.860
Know what I'm trying to say?

11:38.823 --> 11:40.366
We've got air turbulence.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.248
Why'd you decide to join us?

11:51.043 --> 11:52.211
Let's just say...

11:53.087 --> 11:55.131
that I want to get my revenge.

11:58.092 --> 12:00.970
YOKOHAMA TENJIKU'S BOSS
IZANA KUROKAWA

12:02.096 --> 12:07.977
SO BEGAN THE GREATEST
AND FINAL CONFLICT IN TOMAN'S HISTORY

12:12.189 --> 12:14.483
My stomach aches. I gotta use the can.

12:14.483 --> 12:15.818
I gotta pee too.

12:16.318 --> 12:17.528
Okay.

12:17.528 --> 12:20.114
You know, maybe I'll take a crap too.

12:20.114 --> 12:23.242
Yamagishi, that's not how crapping works.

12:23.242 --> 12:25.119
Hey, man. Listen.

12:25.119 --> 12:28.205
I'm going to find a cute chick
and make memories with her.

12:28.205 --> 12:30.207
You just told me that the other day.

12:30.207 --> 12:31.792
Besides, you already have.

12:31.792 --> 12:32.710
Ouch!

12:33.294 --> 12:34.712
Stop right there, asshole!

12:34.712 --> 12:39.049
Can't you even apologize
when you bump into someone?!

12:39.049 --> 12:41.802
Huh? So what if I did bump into you?

12:44.597 --> 12:46.348
What're you whining about?

12:46.348 --> 12:47.892
You want to fight?

12:47.892 --> 12:50.603
You'd better back off, bitches!

12:50.603 --> 12:53.689
We're members of freaking Toman!

12:53.689 --> 12:55.566
What? Toman?

12:55.566 --> 12:59.320
This guy here is captain
of Toman's First Division Attack Squad,

12:59.320 --> 13:01.405
Kazushi Yamagishi!

13:01.405 --> 13:05.159
Now, now, Makoto.
Don't use my name to pick a fight.

13:06.410 --> 13:08.245
- We're sorry!
- We're sorry!

13:12.208 --> 13:14.585
You're with Tokyo Manji Gang, huh?

13:15.669 --> 13:17.505
Who the hell are you people?

13:22.134 --> 13:24.345
It sure is peaceful.

13:24.345 --> 13:26.305
Isn't it, Takemitchy?

13:26.305 --> 13:27.223
Huh?

13:28.140 --> 13:28.974
Yeah.

13:30.518 --> 13:34.104
It's been a week since you got worked up
about being Toman's boss.

13:34.772 --> 13:37.900
But it's not like
we've got any kind of plan.

13:38.526 --> 13:40.110
Will it ever happen?

13:42.196 --> 13:44.406
Are you even listening, Takemitchy?

13:44.406 --> 13:49.495
Chifuyu, I just came up
with an amazing idea.

13:49.495 --> 13:51.330
Huh? An amazing idea?

13:52.122 --> 13:54.291
I know how to get
to the top of the hoodlum world.

13:55.543 --> 13:56.502
Let's go, Chifuyu.

13:57.002 --> 13:58.963
Huh? Where to?

14:00.840 --> 14:02.466
Shibuya Station?

14:02.466 --> 14:04.552
Hold up, Takemitchy.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.428
What's this about
the top of the hoodlum world?

14:06.428 --> 14:10.891
Chifuyu, you own all those sacred texts,
but you didn't realize this?

14:11.475 --> 14:12.601
Sacred texts?

14:12.601 --> 14:14.812
Are you blind or something?

14:16.564 --> 14:18.607
<i>Shonan Junai Gumi.</i>

14:18.607 --> 14:19.942
<i>Bukkomi no Taku.</i>

14:20.484 --> 14:22.987
They taught me everything.

14:22.987 --> 14:23.904
Oh?

14:24.446 --> 14:26.574
Kanagawa's the key to it all!

14:27.074 --> 14:28.075
Ah...

14:28.075 --> 14:28.993
Chifuyu!

14:29.535 --> 14:31.704
To become the greatest of the hoodlums,

14:31.704 --> 14:34.206
I just gotta take down the Yokohama gangs.

14:34.206 --> 14:36.375
<i>Morons sure are incredible.</i>

14:37.042 --> 14:38.544
<i>He's way too easily influenced.</i>

14:39.169 --> 14:41.755
Chifuyu, first we go to Yokohama.

14:41.755 --> 14:43.090
Have fun.

14:43.090 --> 14:44.008
Huh?

14:44.008 --> 14:49.054
It's obvious that all you'll do is
eat pork buns in Chinatown and come back.

14:49.054 --> 14:49.972
I'll pass.

14:49.972 --> 14:51.390
It's a waste of train fare.

14:51.390 --> 14:52.558
Why you!

14:53.225 --> 14:54.351
We're not friends anymore!

14:54.351 --> 14:56.353
Bring back souvenirs.

14:56.854 --> 14:59.607
What an idiot. I'm going home.

14:59.607 --> 15:00.774
- Chifuyu!
- Chifuyu!

15:01.859 --> 15:03.944
What? You already wussed...

15:05.070 --> 15:08.282
Huh? Yamagishi and Makoto?

15:10.117 --> 15:11.994
How'd you get all beat up?

15:14.121 --> 15:14.955
Huh?

15:17.499 --> 15:18.959
So, this is Shibuya, huh?

15:18.959 --> 15:21.545
Ain't much different than our city.

15:21.545 --> 15:22.963
I gotta piss.

15:22.963 --> 15:24.965
I'm broke today, man.

15:24.965 --> 15:27.092
Let's find some hoodlums and mess them up.

15:27.092 --> 15:28.469
We'll shake them down.

15:29.720 --> 15:30.971
<i>Who the heck are these guys?</i>

15:31.555 --> 15:33.182
Move, you freaking punk.

15:34.141 --> 15:35.142
Sorry.

15:36.685 --> 15:40.606
We got jumped by a group of guys
in red high-collar uniforms.

15:42.024 --> 15:44.360
Hey, you're a hoodlum, ain't ya?

15:44.360 --> 15:45.819
What?

15:45.819 --> 15:47.696
Bring that guy we just got.

15:47.696 --> 15:48.906
He looks so weak.

15:52.451 --> 15:53.702
Lookit that guy.

15:54.328 --> 15:56.288
Is he in Toman?

16:02.711 --> 16:03.545
Akkun?!

16:04.296 --> 16:05.798
You idiot, Takemichi.

16:08.342 --> 16:11.303
You're about to become
our fifth Toman victim.

16:14.974 --> 16:16.392
Chifuyu!

16:17.184 --> 16:19.228
Run, Takemitchy and Akkun!

16:21.480 --> 16:22.690
Akkun, get on!

16:26.360 --> 16:27.736
I'll be right there.

16:29.029 --> 16:30.155
Thanks, Chifuyu.

16:30.739 --> 16:32.074
Get back here, damn it!

16:32.866 --> 16:33.909
Out of my way, damn it!

16:36.495 --> 16:37.579
What's going on?

16:38.914 --> 16:41.083
Damn it! What the hell's going on?

16:41.083 --> 16:43.419
Akkun, what the heck's happening?

16:43.419 --> 16:45.421
Who the hell are these guys?

17:03.397 --> 17:05.357
YOKOHAMA TENJIKU'S BIG FOUR
KANJI MOCHIZUKI (ALIAS "MOCCHI")

17:05.357 --> 17:07.401
We'll slaughter everyone
in Tokyo Manji Gang.

17:17.161 --> 17:19.204
Get the hell back here!

17:19.204 --> 17:21.790
Holy shit! What the hell's going on?

17:21.790 --> 17:23.667
Who the hell are these guys?

17:23.667 --> 17:24.793
Takemichi!

17:24.793 --> 17:26.003
This way!

17:26.587 --> 17:27.504
Get in here now!

17:27.504 --> 17:28.881
Yamagishi. Makoto.

17:29.673 --> 17:31.175
Hurry up and lock it!

17:32.551 --> 17:34.219
Thank god.

17:35.846 --> 17:37.097
Open up, damn it!

17:37.097 --> 17:39.141
You aren't getting away from us!

17:39.141 --> 17:40.392
Oh, shit.

17:40.392 --> 17:41.685
Out the back!

17:41.685 --> 17:44.021
Takemichi, let's go
before they surround us.

17:47.149 --> 17:48.150
Where's Chifuyu?

17:48.734 --> 17:51.445
He'll join us later.
He's tough so he'll be fine.

17:56.492 --> 17:57.326
Clear.

17:59.995 --> 18:00.996
I'm sorry, Takemichi.

18:01.497 --> 18:03.957
It's my fault this happened.

18:03.957 --> 18:06.001
Huh? Your fault?

18:06.502 --> 18:09.797
Those guys are
the Tenjiku gang from Yokohama.

18:10.714 --> 18:13.383
I don't know why,
but they're coming after Toman.

18:13.884 --> 18:17.679
When I said we're in Toman,
they suddenly attacked us.

18:18.722 --> 18:20.724
Akkun played decoy to mislead them.

18:21.683 --> 18:24.269
But we got separated
from Takuya while escaping.

18:24.269 --> 18:25.187
Really?

18:25.938 --> 18:27.523
Takemichi...

18:28.107 --> 18:28.982
Akkun.

18:30.609 --> 18:32.361
Those guys are bad news.

18:33.028 --> 18:39.034
I heard 300 members
of Tenjiku came to Tokyo today.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.911
What? 300?!

18:41.620 --> 18:42.830
<i>Chifuyu's in danger.</i>

18:44.456 --> 18:46.041
Akkun, can you walk?

18:46.500 --> 18:48.001
Yeah.

18:48.001 --> 18:48.919
Here.

18:49.419 --> 18:50.254
Thanks.

18:50.838 --> 18:53.507
You guys, go to Toman's hideout.

18:53.966 --> 18:56.218
There's sure to be other members there.

18:56.218 --> 18:57.719
Huh? What about you?

18:58.303 --> 18:59.513
I forgot something.

18:59.513 --> 19:01.014
I'll meet up with you soon.

19:03.308 --> 19:06.812
<i>Damn Chifuyu,
acting like he had it under control.</i>

19:06.812 --> 19:12.943
<i>He played the decoy even though he knew
he was facing those badass Tenjiku guys.</i>

19:12.943 --> 19:15.362
Chifuyu! I hope you're all--

19:18.115 --> 19:21.160
Look who came waltzing back, you moron!

19:23.203 --> 19:24.121
Take this!

19:29.376 --> 19:30.294
Shit!

19:31.795 --> 19:33.005
Die!

19:33.005 --> 19:34.756
Not so fast!

19:40.012 --> 19:41.096
Akkun?

19:41.889 --> 19:42.973
Captain!

19:44.349 --> 19:46.393
Did you think we'd hold you back?

19:46.393 --> 19:49.646
We're not just
the Mizo Middle Five anymore.

19:50.314 --> 19:53.734
We're in Toman's First Division,
and you're our captain!

19:56.028 --> 19:58.280
You're going to save Chifuyu, right?

19:58.280 --> 20:00.115
We can't let you go alone.

20:03.118 --> 20:05.204
- We're all part of Toman too!
- We're all part of Toman too!

20:05.204 --> 20:07.289
We don't abandon our friends!

20:07.789 --> 20:09.541
Goddamn it!

20:09.541 --> 20:12.169
Those 300 dudes aren't shit!

20:12.169 --> 20:14.630
We'll open an escape route!

20:14.630 --> 20:16.381
Here we go, Captain!

20:19.009 --> 20:21.887
Hell yeah!

20:45.160 --> 20:46.578
It's over for you.

20:47.704 --> 20:48.580
Damn it.

20:49.790 --> 20:51.583
They just keep coming.

20:52.167 --> 20:53.543
I'm done for.

20:54.127 --> 20:55.462
I can't even stand.

20:58.632 --> 21:00.425
<i>Who the hell are these guys?</i>

21:00.425 --> 21:02.928
<i>I've never heard of Tenjiku.</i>

21:03.637 --> 21:07.015
<i>These guys were never
part of the past before.</i>

21:11.228 --> 21:13.522
FIRST GENERATION YOKOHAMA TENJIKU

21:24.533 --> 21:27.202
I bet you have no idea what's going on.

21:29.246 --> 21:30.080
Huh?

21:35.043 --> 21:36.128
Kisaki!

21:42.175 --> 21:44.636
Hey there, hero.

21:45.304 --> 21:46.138
Huh?

21:47.014 --> 21:48.015
<i>Hero?</i>

21:49.349 --> 21:52.019
Let the Kanto Incident begin.

22:01.320 --> 22:02.154
<i>Don't tell me</i>

22:03.363 --> 22:04.281
<i>he's...</i>

22:06.533 --> 22:10.954
TOKYO REVENGERS

23:38.375 --> 23:40.377
Translation by Brian Athey
